WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.527
Apollo Q Labs. Level four, module four: your written plan and journal.

2
00:00:06.827 --> 00:00:20.652
As in module one, options magnify small moves, and many traders cap the max loss on any single trade at a small slice of the account, often one to two percent. Check the Capital at risk card before you place a trade.

3
00:00:20.952 --> 00:00:30.596
As in the dashboard lesson, max profit and max loss are the best and worst outcome at expiration. Unlimited means one side has no cap.

4
00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:35.591
Write your plan, the rules for a trade, before you open it, not after it goes wrong.

5
00:00:35.591 --> 00:00:43.123
Decide exit rules, when you would get out, in advance, so they are less likely to be driven by emotion, how you feel in the moment.

6
00:00:43.123 --> 00:00:48.969
A basic plan includes the maximum risk per trade, the most you are willing to lose on one trade.

7
00:00:49.269 --> 00:00:56.844
Practice the plan first with fake money, also called paper trading: the same steps, without risking real cash.

8
00:00:56.844 --> 00:01:04.888
That is practice, not proof. Real fill prices, the price your order actually gets, and real emotions can differ.

9
00:01:05.188 --> 00:01:12.464
Keep a journal, your record of past trades. A useful entry records why you entered, the plan, the result, and the lesson.

10
00:01:12.464 --> 00:01:16.561
Writing down reasons and results helps you find repeat mistakes.

11
00:01:16.561 --> 00:01:25.395
After a string of losses, stick to your risk limits and review the journal. Do not raise position size, how much you put in, to chase those losses.

12
00:01:25.695 --> 00:01:40.843
Recap: write the rules before you trade, practice with fake money, and review your journal. Many traders keep each trade’s max loss to a small slice of the account, and check max profit, max loss, and capital at risk first.

13
00:01:40.843 --> 00:01:44.705
Next, read the lessons, then take the six question quiz.

